+### Tune-up ("Komplet")
+
+**Health → Tune-up** (`/health/tune-up`, 0.146.0+) runs every maintenance
+step debcontrol can, one after another, on one machine, a group or every
+machine the account can see. A machine's health panel (Overview) has a
+**Tune-up** button that opens the form with that machine chosen.
+
+| # | Step | Can be turned off |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Refresh facts, packages, services and update readiness. If the machine doesn't answer, the tune-up of that machine stops here | no |
+| 2 | System update: `apt update`, `full-upgrade`, `autoremove`, `autoclean` (the same update run as the Updates tab, optionally with a Proxmox snapshot first) | yes |
+| 3 | Check Docker images for newer versions | no |
+| 4 | Update every container with a newer image (debcontrol's own are left alone) | yes |
+| 5 | Clean up Docker: `docker system prune -a`, stopped containers, unused images, networks and build cache. **Volumes are never removed** | yes |
+| 6 | Scan every image for vulnerabilities (Trivy/Grype) | yes |
+| 7 | [Security audit](Security-Audit): Lynis, installed or updated first, and the vps-audit checks | yes |
+| 8 | Refresh everything again, take a monitoring sample, evaluate health | no |
+| 9 | Reboot, only on machines that need it | off by default; needs `action.power` |
+
+Docker steps are skipped on a machine without Docker. Starting or
+stopping needs `action.updates` (audited as `machine.tune_up.start` /
+`machine.tune_up.cancel`).
+
+![A tune-up of two machines](images/tune-up.png)
+
+**How it runs** (`app.services.tune_up`, `app.tasks.tune_up`): one
+`TuneUpRun` per machine under one batch id, each followed by its own
+Celery task. A step that is a job of its own (the update run, Docker
+jobs, the audit) is started through the same code as its button and
+waited for, its id kept in the step. At most **4 machines** run at once;
+the rest wait their turn. debcontrol's own host and the hypervisor under
+it go last and are never rebooted. A sweep every 2 minutes
+(`reconcile-tune-up-runs`) hands a run whose task stopped (a worker
+restart) to a new task, which skips finished steps and waits for the one
+under way instead of starting it again. **Stop** ends waiting machines
+at once; a running one stops after its current step.
+
+Also as a [scheduled action](Scheduling-and-Power#maintenance-actions)
+(`tune_up`) and through the REST API: `GET`/`POST /api/v1/tune-ups`,
+`GET /api/v1/tune-ups/{batch_id}`, `POST /api/v1/tune-ups/{batch_id}/cancel`.
+
